//! Pascal: `program NewThroughPointer;`

// Pascal programs often declare things they never use, or assign a
// variable before reading it; that's fine, so don't warn about it.
#![allow(unused_variables, unused_assignments, dead_code)]

use pascrust_runtime::prelude::*;

// New and Dispose through a Pointer cast to a typed pointer: the record
// is kept in the Pointer, and read back through the same cast. A cast
// to the pointer's own type changes nothing.

/// Pascal: `^TNode`
